WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:01.770
- All right, y'all, we have time

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.300
for one more uplifting story.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.311
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:04.311 --> 00:00:07.140
(rock music)

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.420
Police officers often find unique ways

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:10.560
to connect with the community,

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:12.030
but probably none are as unique

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.956
as this officer from Maryland.

00:00:13.956 --> 00:00:17.373
("Star Spangled Banner")

00:00:28.224 --> 00:00:29.340
(audience clapping)

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.173
So beautiful.

00:00:30.173 --> 00:00:31.830
Officer Alexander Strachan

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:33.960
of the Prince George's
County Police Department

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:35.760
has been playing violin all his life,

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.110
beautifully, might I add.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:39.150
He says music is a
bridge to the community.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:40.260
I could not agree more.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:41.169
Let's get him in here everybody.

00:00:41.169 --> 00:00:43.724
All right, Officer
Strachan, how you doing?

00:00:43.724 --> 00:00:45.090
(audience cheering)

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:45.923
- Hi Kelly.

00:00:45.923 --> 00:00:47.310
It's so nice to meet you.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:48.210
- Nice to meet you as well.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:50.760
Wow, first of all, you
have a beautiful smile.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:52.080
My goodness.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:53.250
Well, you only recently.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:54.083
- Well, thank you.

00:00:54.083 --> 00:00:54.916
- Yeah, you're welcome.

00:00:54.916 --> 00:00:57.840
You only recently joined the
police force, is that right?

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.210
- Yes, I joined about two years ago.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:02.820
It's been such an honor to be a officer

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.410
for the Prince George's County Police.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.660
I've had the opportunity
to be able to play violin

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:09.570
in uniform, so it's so
neat to be able to help

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:11.310
be a bridge for the community.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:13.140
I get to go, and that was
at the Wellness House.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:15.810
I get to play different
communities and charities

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:17.460
and represent the police department.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:19.110
Maybe we'll go in nursing homes

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:21.660
and it's so cool because
people see the gun and badge

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:23.640
and think, "Well, what's going on?"

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:25.440
And they see me playing the violin

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.030
and they're like, "Oh, this is so cool."

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:30.030
So, it's an amazing
opportunity and such an honor.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:31.710
I'm incredibly blessed.

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:34.560
- It's a cool way for kids, especially,

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.840
to see law enforcement
in a different light.

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.730
So how did you, was it your grandparents?

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:40.800
Is that what started you
in the nursing homes?

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.633
- Yes.

00:01:41.633 --> 00:01:45.270
So my grandmother, she had
Alzheimer's and breast cancer

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:48.450
and music was something
that brought her back to me

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:50.430
despite the fog of the Alzheimer's.

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:52.500
And it was that amazing connection

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.140
that I could have being
able to play music for her,

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.210
especially the day before she passed away.

00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:00.300
And I wanted to continue
that work in nursing homes

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.370
and for people in hospice as well.

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:03.660
Playing for terminally ill children

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:05.520
and adults by the bedside.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.110
- That is such a cool thing, man.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:08.430
You're so rad.

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:10.630
Can we hear a little
bit of "Amazing Grace"?

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:14.010
- Absolutely, it's one of
my grandma's favorites.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:15.153
- I love it, mine too.

00:02:17.918 --> 00:02:20.751
("Amazing Grace")

00:02:48.277 --> 00:02:51.090
Wow, I love the vents, the slight vents.

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:52.080
Man, that's so good.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:53.850
Thank you so much.

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:54.840
Thank you, Officer Strachan.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.439
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:56.439 --> 00:02:58.440
(audience cheering)

00:02:58.440 --> 00:02:59.610
That's not all though.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:02.130
Our season long partner Pilot
Pen, the makers of FriXion,

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:04.260
the go-to erasable pen of
"The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:06.660
are inspired by your
dedication to your community

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:07.950
and the memory of your grandmother.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.170
So they're gonna write
you a check for $1,000

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:12.587
on your behalf to the Wellness House

00:03:12.587 --> 00:03:13.420
of Annapolis.
- Thank you so much.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:16.080
- Which is dedicated to serving families

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:17.730
who have been touched by cancer.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.198
Thank you so much.

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:20.541
- Thank you.

00:03:20.541 --> 00:03:21.870
- Have a blessed day.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:24.090
And thank you to everybody,
all our guests this hour:

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:27.090
Hannah Waddingham, Reid Scott,
Garrett and Emily Coffman.

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:27.923
Y'all have a great day,

00:03:27.923 --> 00:03:29.440
and if it's not, try and change it.

